{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"209","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Multicolored Marbles"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarpus plays with red and blue marbles. He put "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" marbles from the left to the right in a row. As it turned out, the marbles form a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"zebroid"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A non-empty sequence of red and blue marbles is a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"zebroid"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if the colors of the marbles in this sequence alternate. For example, sequences ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"red; blue; red"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":") and ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"blue"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":") are zebroids and sequence ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"red; red"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":") is not a zebroid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now Polycarpus wonders, how many ways there are to pick a zebroid "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subsequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" from this sequence. Help him solve the problem, find the number of ways modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(109 + 7)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 106)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of marbles in Polycarpus's sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single number — the answer to the problem modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000000007"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(109 + 7)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"11\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the first test sample. Let's assume that Polycarpus initially had sequence ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"red; blue; red"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"), so there are six ways to pick a zebroid: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" pick the first marble; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" pick the second marble; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" pick the third marble; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" pick the first and second marbles; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" pick the second and third marbles; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" pick the first, second and third marbles. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proven that if Polycarpus picks ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"blue; red; blue"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":") as the initial sequence, the number of ways won't change."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"209A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/209/problem/A"}